<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>

    <!-- dotnet tool install -g Roslynaut. The package holds the publish output, so the helper hosts beside the server too. -->
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>roslynaut</ToolCommandName>
    <RollForward>Major</RollForward>
    <Version>0.4.0</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
- decompile, assembly_asm, symbol_asm (without pgoWorkload) and type_layout keep their results in a cache under %TEMP%/Roslynaut/Cache, by the content of the assembly and of the assemblies, .deps.json and .runtimeconfig.json next to it (or the dependencies of code compiled from source), and for listings the runtime that compiles them. A later call for the same code, from this or another server, answers at once instead of decompiling again or starting the JIT host.
- --install run through dnx registers dotnet dnx with the version that runs (such as Roslynaut@0.4.0 --yes), which downloads it again when the NuGet caches were cleared. It registered the copy in the NuGet packages folder, which clearing the caches deleted, so the agent could no longer start the server or its hooks.
- --install on Windows writes the paths of its commands with forward slashes. Agents that run a command through a shell, as Claude Code runs its hooks through Git Bash, read the backslashes as escapes, and the hooks failed.
- The server leaves out the tools that cannot work, and says why on standard error: evaluate and benchmark without ROSLYNAUT_ALLOW_EVALUATE=true, and the debug tools without netcoredbg. Agents saw them, and calling them failed.
- --install with --enable-tools or --disable-tools registers the server with those options, so the agent gets only those tools. It registered all tools.
- --install with --no-hooks registers the server alone: Claude Code gets no hooks and OpenCode no plugin, and those an earlier installation added are removed. The other agents get no hook either way.
- The server instructions fit in the 4,000 characters Claude Code keeps of them. It cut them off after the packages tools, so agents lacked the guidance for the profiling, memory, process, debugger and quality tools.
- Tool schemas take about 7% less of agents' context: optional parameters leave null out of their types and defaults, and the symbol path description they share is shorter.
- The Claude Code hooks give each hint once per session, and again after it starts anew or compacts. They repeated it on every read, grep or edit of C# code.
- --tool-descriptions and --field-descriptions serve the tools' descriptions or their parameters' in full, as their first sentence (short), in caveman style (terse, keeping identifiers and search keywords) or not at all (none), for less of agents' context, and the new tool explain_tool gives them in full for the tools an agent calls. --install registers the server with them.
- definition and signature_help expand &lt;inheritdoc/&gt; in the documentation they return: with its cref, path, or the member the symbol overrides or implements, its base types and interfaces. An undocumented method, property or event that overrides or implements another gets that one's documentation. They returned the tag as it was, and nothing for an undocumented override or implementation.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>Wesley Baartman</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Wesley Baartman</Copyright>
    <Description>An MCP server that exposes Roslyn and MSBuild to agents: navigation, analysis, refactoring, builds and tests, IL/JIT disassembly, decompilation, process inspection and debugging of C# projects.</Description>
    <PackageTags>mcp;roslyn;msbuild;csharp;agents;opencode;claude;llm;agentic</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/CptWesley/Roslynaut</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/CptWesley/Roslynaut</RepositoryUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Release'">
    <RuntimeIdentifiers>win-x64;win-arm64;linux-x64;linux-arm64;linux-musl-x64;linux-musl-arm64;osx-x64;osx-arm64;any</RuntimeIdentifiers>
    <PublishReadyToRun>true</PublishReadyToRun>
    <UseAppHost>false</UseAppHost>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Roslynaut.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="BitFaster.Caching" Version="2.6.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="Buildalyzer" Version="9.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="ICSharpCode.Decompiler" Version="11.1.0.9782" />
    <PackageReference Include="LiteDB" Version="5.0.21" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.Features" Version="5.12.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.Workspaces" Version="5.12.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.VisualBasic.Workspaces" Version="5.12.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Diagnostics.NETCore.Client" Version="0.2.750501" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Diagnostics.Runtime" Version="4.2.751201" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Diagnostics.Tracing.TraceEvent" Version="3.2.5" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection" Version="10.0.13" />
    <PackageReference Include="ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore" Version="2.2.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Mono.Cecil" Version="0.11.6" />
    <PackageReference Include="MSBuild.StructuredLogger" Version="2.3.246" />
    <PackageReference Include="NuGet.Credentials" Version="7.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="NuGet.ProjectModel" Version="7.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="NuGet.Protocol" Version="7.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.CommandLine" Version="2.0.14" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Xml" Version="10.0.13" />
    <PackageReference Include="Tomlyn" Version="2.11.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Roslynaut.CallCounter\Roslynaut.CallCounter.csproj" GlobalPropertiesToRemove="RuntimeIdentifier;SelfContained" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Roslynaut.JitHost\Roslynaut.JitHost.csproj" GlobalPropertiesToRemove="RuntimeIdentifier;SelfContained" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Roslynaut.ScriptHost\Roslynaut.ScriptHost.csproj" GlobalPropertiesToRemove="RuntimeIdentifier;SelfContained" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
